WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.912
Anika: The timeout cleanup path misses release. Ten cancellations retained ten borrowed connections.

2
00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:13.584
Hannah: Did normal requests release them correctly? We need the successful control too.

3
00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:20.665
Raj: Yes, normal requests return them consistently. That confirms this connection leak now.

4
00:00:20.665 --> 00:00:28.057
Priya: Okay, test exceptions as well, right? Maybe cancellation isn't the sole broken branch.

5
00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:34.417
Lukas: And check open transaction cleanup separately. Returning a dirty connection isn't safe.

6
00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:40.849
Anika: I'm on it with structured cleanup. Release follows transaction outcome handling now.

7
00:00:40.849 --> 00:00:47.833
Hannah: The smoke test must include timeouts. Healthy requests alone won't cover this.

8
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:54.866
Raj: Query execution time remains a separate issue. Reports still need their filter reviewed.

9
00:00:54.866 --> 00:01:01.226
Lukas: Keep that action item after mitigation. Don't bundle an untested query rewrite.

10
00:01:01.226 --> 00:01:07.970
Priya: So, stage the cleanup fix first. Reports resume only after separate validation.

